From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:37:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(rest): Rest and Charge score each night against its
 personal sleep need and regularity

Upstream computed a personal need and a regularity in the analysis pass but only
handed them to DayResult.rest, which nothing reads: every stored Rest, every Charge
and every screen ran on a fixed 8 h need and a neutral 0.5 regularity, while the Sleep
screen showed the need in three other ways (the debt's upper quartile over all days,
the "Hours vs Needed" tile's mean floored at 7.5 h, the detail graph's own mean).

One resolver, VictorSleepNeed: night D's need is the upper quartile (age floor, 9.5 h
cap, population default under 7 nights) of the 90 nights with sleep before D; its
regularity is 1 - CV of the 28 nights up to D (upstream's Wave 0 definition). Both
come from the merged daily rows, so nothing new is stored and no schema changes.

- Analysis pass: applyPersonalRest, after the scoring loop, resolves from the merged
  history as it will read after the pass (WhoopRepository.daysMergedWith), rewrites the
  window's stored Rest, recomputes its Charge with that Rest, emits the Charge trace
  (moved out of the loop) and a "rest personal" Sleep trace line, and rewrites an older
  stored Rest that no longer matches its night. Older Charge is left as scored.
- Readers: Sleep screen (Rest, need, % of need, debt series and ledger, trend need,
  per-night regularity graph, the reads-short caveat), the hero, Coupled, the weekly
  digest, the widget, the morning recap, Today's Charge drivers and the resolved
  series' daily fallback all read VictorSleepNeed; a source guard test fails on any
  new Rest or need computed outside it.
- The Consistency tile keeps its bedtime regularity (needs session onsets, not rows).
- Android-only fork patch: the Swift twin is not changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
